WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.420
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online TOEIC preparation.

2
00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:09.176
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.476 --> 00:00:18.758
Unit seventeen: Part 7: Notices, Ads and Forms. Today you will scan advertisements, notices, forms and tables for specific information.

4
00:00:19.058 --> 00:00:21.733
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:22.667 --> 00:00:26.050
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:26.917 --> 00:00:27.836
Notice.

7
00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:30.989
Notice means a short public message.

8
00:00:31.583 --> 00:00:33.293
The notice is on the board.

9
00:00:33.883 --> 00:00:36.454
Your turn. Say: Notice.

10
00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:40.243
Notice.

11
00:00:40.983 --> 00:00:42.286
Advertisement.

12
00:00:43.283 --> 00:00:46.096
Advertisement means a message promoting a product.

13
00:00:46.683 --> 00:00:48.776
The advertisement offers a sale.

14
00:00:49.383 --> 00:00:52.338
Your turn. Say: Advertisement.

15
00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:56.468
Advertisement.

16
00:00:57.217 --> 00:00:57.869
Form.

17
00:00:58.883 --> 00:01:01.417
Form means a document with spaces to fill in.

18
00:01:02.017 --> 00:01:03.262
Complete the form.

19
00:01:03.850 --> 00:01:05.980
Your turn. Say: Form.

20
00:01:08.833 --> 00:01:09.602
Form.

21
00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:11.328
Eligible.

22
00:01:12.317 --> 00:01:14.560
Eligible means allowed to take part.

23
00:01:15.150 --> 00:01:16.941
Only members are eligible.

24
00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:20.156
Your turn. Say: Eligible.

25
00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:23.989
Eligible.

26
00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:25.832
Expire.

27
00:01:26.817 --> 00:01:28.363
Expire means to end.

28
00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:31.217
The offer expires on June 30.

29
00:01:31.817 --> 00:01:34.167
Your turn. Say: Expire.

30
00:01:37.033 --> 00:01:37.953
Expire.

31
00:01:38.717 --> 00:01:39.404
Fee.

32
00:01:40.417 --> 00:01:42.706
Fee means money paid for a service.

33
00:01:43.317 --> 00:01:45.049
A small fee applies.

34
00:01:45.650 --> 00:01:48.140
Your turn. Say: Fee.

35
00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:51.780
Fee.

36
00:01:52.517 --> 00:01:53.448
Warranty.

37
00:01:54.450 --> 00:01:56.868
Warranty means a promise to repair a product.

38
00:01:57.483 --> 00:01:59.378
The warranty lasts two years.

39
00:01:59.983 --> 00:02:02.647
Your turn. Say: Warranty.

40
00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:06.582
Warranty.

41
00:02:07.317 --> 00:02:08.190
Scan.

42
00:02:09.183 --> 00:02:11.624
Scan means to look quickly for a detail.

43
00:02:12.217 --> 00:02:13.589
Scan for the date.

44
00:02:14.183 --> 00:02:16.418
Your turn. Say: Scan.

45
00:02:19.267 --> 00:02:20.245
Scan.

46
00:02:21.033 --> 00:02:24.916
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:29.003
Visal, how are these texts different from emails?

48
00:02:30.117 --> 00:02:39.433
Notices, ads and forms are not read from start to finish. You scan them for specific details such as dates, prices, conditions and contact information.

49
00:02:40.517 --> 00:02:41.866
How do I scan well?

50
00:02:42.950 --> 00:02:53.869
Read the question first, find keywords such as expires or fee, and look for them in the text. Read the sentence around the keyword to be sure of the condition.

51
00:02:54.983 --> 00:02:57.157
What conditions are commonly tested?

52
00:02:58.250 --> 00:03:09.180
Look for words like only, unless, before and except. They limit who can take part or when an offer applies, so an answer that ignores them may be wrong.

53
00:03:10.333 --> 00:03:11.834
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:12.683 --> 00:03:17.260
Grammar focus: Strategy: scan with keywords, then read the condition.

55
00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:18.805
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:19.517 --> 00:03:21.853
The offer expires on June 30.

57
00:03:22.750 --> 00:03:25.168
Only members are eligible for the discount.

58
00:03:26.133 --> 00:03:32.092
Read the question first, scan for keywords, and always check the condition words like only, unless and before.

59
00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:36.977
Be careful! Don't say: I ignore words like only and unless.

60
00:03:38.933 --> 00:03:41.618
Say: I check the condition words.

61
00:03:41.918 --> 00:03:43.174
Conditions matter.

62
00:03:43.967 --> 00:03:46.712
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:47.500 --> 00:03:49.116
A Sale Advertisement.

64
00:03:49.416 --> 00:03:52.554
An advertisement offers twenty percent off laptops.

65
00:03:53.567 --> 00:03:56.054
The discount is only for members of the store club.

66
00:03:57.067 --> 00:03:59.101
The offer expires on June 30.

67
00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:03.911
A small delivery fee applies to orders under fifty dollars.

68
00:04:04.900 --> 00:04:07.550
Every laptop comes with a two-year warranty.

69
00:04:08.633 --> 00:04:12.670
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:13.517 --> 00:04:15.702
Notices and ads are read by blank.

71
00:04:16.002 --> 00:04:20.039
A, translating. B, memorising. C, scanning.

72
00:04:23.600 --> 00:04:25.298
The answer is C: scanning.

73
00:04:26.450 --> 00:04:27.974
Who gets the discount?

74
00:04:28.274 --> 00:04:31.846
A, club members. B, everyone. C, no one.

75
00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:37.748
The answer is A: club members.

76
00:04:38.883 --> 00:04:40.569
The warranty lasts blank.

77
00:04:40.869 --> 00:04:44.523
A, ten years. B, two years. C, one month.

78
00:04:48.067 --> 00:04:50.438
The answer is B: two years.

79
00:04:51.583 --> 00:04:53.409
When does the offer expire?

80
00:04:53.709 --> 00:04:57.594
A, June 3. B, July 1. C, June 30.

81
00:05:01.133 --> 00:05:03.098
The answer is C: June 30.

82
00:05:04.250 --> 00:05:06.296
Condition words include blank.

83
00:05:06.596 --> 00:05:11.434
A, only and unless. B, apple and orange. C, red and blue.

84
00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:18.068
The answer is A: only and unless.

85
00:05:19.267 --> 00:05:22.267
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:23.117 --> 00:05:25.766
How do you find information in an advertisement?

87
00:05:34.550 --> 00:05:36.050
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:36.350 --> 00:05:49.628
I read the question first and choose keywords. Then I scan the advertisement for them and read the sentence around each keyword. I pay special attention to words like only and unless because they set conditions.

89
00:05:49.928 --> 00:05:51.603
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:52.517 --> 00:05:58.548
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: scan with keywords, then read the condition.

91
00:05:58.848 --> 00:06:02.881
Today's value is attention. Look carefully and listen well.

92
00:06:03.181 --> 00:06:05.880
See you in Unit eighteen. Goodbye!

93
00:06:06.180 --> 00:06:10.179
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

